      "practice_mapping_verdict": "PASS",
      "summary": "247 CMR 9.01(1), (2), (5), (9)-(14), (18)-(21) and 9.03 are quoted accurately against the current December 2024 text. The descriptions of paragraphs (3), (4), (6)-(8) and (15)-(17), taught elsewhere, are accurate. The 247 CMR 2.00 definitions and the absence of a definition of licensee are verified, as is the 247 CMR 10.03(1)(m) cross-reference. The REMS paragraph does not overstate federal law: 21 U.S.C. s. 355-1(f)(3)(B) lets a REMS restrict dispensing to certified pharmacies, and s. 352(y) places compliance on the responsible person, which the section does not contradict. The statements about M.G.L. c. 112, ss. 65G and 24H, c. 13, s. 9(a) and St. 2022, c. 177, s. 36 are accurate. Program terms are attributed and dated, and the statute is kept separate. One Medium defect: the section teaches the manual's no-practice status at application and enrollment but omits the program's return-to-practice path during participation, which misdescribes what admission does to practice. One Low pinpoint slip: the s. 65G(e) proviso is cited as (g). All six practice questions are answerable from the section and are not contradicted by it."
